enotype, fitness and replication capacity of human immunodeficiency v&#x000ed;rus type with B and C proteases.</article-title><source>Antimicrob Agents Chemother</source><volume>48</volume><fpage>3552</fpage><lpage>3555</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15328124</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000730-Abecasis1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Abecasis</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Deforche</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Snoeck</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bacheler</surname><given-names>LT</given-names></name><name><surname>McKenna</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Protease mutation M89I/V is linked to therapy failure in patients infected with the HIV-1 non-B subtypes C, F or G.</article-title><source>AIDS</source><volume>19</volume><fpage>1799</fpage><lpage>1806</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16227787</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000730-Grossman1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grossman</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Istomin</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Averbuch</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Lorber</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Risenberg</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Genetic variation at NNRTI resistance-associated positions in patients infected with HIV-1 subtype C.</article-title><source>AIDS</source><volume>18</volume><fpage>909</fpage><lpage>915</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15060438</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000730-Brindeiro1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brindeiro</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Diaz</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Sabino</surname><given-names>EC</given-names></name><name><surname>Morgado</surname><given-names>MG</given-names></name><name><surname>Pires</surname><given-names>IL</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Brazilian Network for HIV Drug Resistance Surveillance (HIV-BResNet): a survey of chronically infected individuals.</article-title><source>AIDS</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>1063</fpage><lpage>1069</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12700457</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000730-Soares1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Soares</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>De Oliveira</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Brindeiro</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Diaz</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Sabino</surname><given-names>EC</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>A specific subtype C of human immunodeficiency virus type 1 circulates in Brazil.</article-title><source>AIDS</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>11</fpage><lpage>21</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12478065</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000730-Teixeira1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Teixeira</surname><given-names>PR</given-names></name><name><surname>Vitoria</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Barcarolo</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Antiretroviral treatment in resource-poor settings: the Brazilian experience.</article-title><source>AIDS</source><volume>18</volume><issue>Suppl 3</issue><fpage>S5</fpage><lpage>S7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15322477</pub-id></citat